  "Source": "C. Williams, G. Rughoobur, A. J. Flewitt, and T. D. Wilkinson, \"Single-step fabrication of thin-film linear variable bandpass filters based on metal-insulator-metal geometry,\" Appl. Opt. 55, 9237-9241 (2016). doi:10.1364/AO.55.009237 - Fig. 4 caption (MgF2 ~155 nm from quartz monitor); Sec. 3 text: Ag (25 nm): MgF2 : Ag (25 nm)",
  "Notes": "Single-wavelength MIM transmission colour filter (blue curve of Fig. 4b)\nSpecification: First-order MIM Fabry-Perot transmission band in the visible; thickness from quartz crystal monitor (~155 nm).\nReported: Measured R and T spectra in Fig. 4b only (plotted, no numeric peak wavelength or amplitude given in text).\nNotes: Symmetric stack so order is unambiguous; incident medium assumed air (normal incidence measurement through microscope). Substrate is a 0.7 mm glass slide; the paper's simulations model the substrate as SiO2 (Palik), so SiO2 used. Ag optical constants: CRC data in the paper's FDTD (not tabulated) - use a standard Ag dataset. MgF2 modelled as n=1.38 non-dispersive in the paper. No encapsulation layer on these Fig. 4 samples. Thicknesses are approximate ('~').\nLayers from Fig. 4 caption (MgF2 ~155 nm from quartz monitor); Sec. 3 text: Ag (25 nm): MgF2 : Ag (25 nm); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
